#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115100 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115271 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6af60bcc-de12-52a1-b0b0-9485ed497126" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Rational Expression by Factoring a Difference of Squares in the Numerator"}] :question/id #uuid "1eaa26ba-0958-58db-9f30-35a33f98f2d2" :question/math-academy-id "e-5121" :question/problem "Simplify $\\dfrac {x^2 - 9} {(x + 3)(x+2)}.$" :question/worked-solution "The numerator is a difference of squares. If we factor it and then cancel out any common factors that appear in both the numerator and the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel}\n\t\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {x^2 - 9} {(x + 3)(x+2)}  & = \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac {(x + 3)(x - 3)} {(x + 3)(x+2)}&=\\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac {\\cancel{(x + 3)}(x - 3)} {\\cancel{(x + 3)}(x+2)}&=\\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac {x - 3} {x+2} &. \\\t\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115101 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115272 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22de4ff5-a317-5d89-a9da-80d40648f2e1" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Rational Expression by Factoring a Second-Order Polynomial in the Numerator"}] :question/id #uuid "fb69899e-6aee-5128-973e-e19792a1cbdb" :question/math-academy-id "e-5122" :question/problem "What is $\\dfrac {x^2 + x - 6} {x-2}$ reduced to lowest terms?" :question/worked-solution "The numerator can be factored as $x^2+x-6= (x+3)(x-2).$ Cancelling out any common factors that appear in the numerator and the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+x-6}{x-2} & = \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)(x-2)}{x-2} & = \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)\\cancel{(x-2)}}{\\cancel{(x-2)}} & = \\\\ \\frac{x+3}{1} & = \\\\ x+3 & .\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115102 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca7321f2-f17f-5d22-a0d1-02720b3a6dc5" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Rational Expression by Factoring a Second-Order Polynomial in the Denominator"}] :question/id #uuid "fd181873-1190-5ffa-b2aa-c7eb68c1255c" :question/math-academy-id "e-5123" :question/problem "Simplify $\\dfrac{4(a+b)} {2a^2+4ab+2b^2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we take out a factor of $2$ from the denominator, and then use the polynomial factorization $a^2+2ab+b^2 = (a+b)^2.$ Cancelling out any common factors that appear in both the numerator and the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel}\n\t\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac{4(a+b)} {2a^2+4ab+2b^2}\n\t\t&=\\dfrac{4(a+b)} {2\\left(a^2+2ab+b^2\\right)} \\\n                &=\\dfrac{2\\cdot 2\\cdot(a+b)} {2(a+b)(a+b)} \\\n\t\t&=\\dfrac{\\cancel{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot\\cancel{(a+b)}} {\\cancel{2}\\cancel{(a+b)}(a+b)}\\\n\t\t&=\\dfrac {2} {a+b}.\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115104 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115279 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4030a2b3-34aa-5d00-bd95-e382ec781b20" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Rational Expression by Factoring Second-Order Polynomials in Both the Numerator and Denominator"}] :question/id #uuid "1e777ba3-6a10-5c47-b069-ee33a6892a98" :question/math-academy-id "e-5313" :question/problem "Simplify $\\dfrac{x^2-4}{x^2-5x+6}.$" :question/worked-solution "We factor the numerator and denominator, canceling out any common factors that appear in both.\n\n![](images/39/39c702fb9697e87abfb8bbfb1a4bfbec813a0f4ffbe47d3ea90b56adfdd371a0.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529169 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca7321f2-f17f-5d22-a0d1-02720b3a6dc5" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Rational Expression by Factoring a Second-Order Polynomial in the Denominator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f13fc29-f05e-5620-98a4-db8b5e91ff7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{t-15}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528418} {:answer/id #uuid "418dfecf-ec3a-5583-9851-3ff2cb427404" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{t-5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528469} {:answer/id #uuid "775d37e2-5c7a-56f2-a453-a2f9bac2ad89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{t+5}{t-5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528577} {:answer/id #uuid "9a600d81-113a-5888-96a7-e80b763e08ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3t-15}{t-5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528667} {:answer/id #uuid "b2fc03f0-1570-50e3-8044-f6d69f974008" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t-5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528737}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2fc03f0-1570-50e3-8044-f6d69f974008" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t-5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528737} :answer-field/id #uuid "32d5cbfd-428a-5053-acb7-ffa3e900ce28" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528971}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c85a34c5-6e9b-5e37-9be6-8bd5b320956b" :question/math-academy-id "q-113063" :question/problem "Simplify $\\frac{3t-15}{3{t}^{2}-30t+75}.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we take out a factor of $3$ from the numerator and from the denominator, and then use the polynomial factorization ${t}^{2}-10t+25=(t-5)^{2}.$ Canceling out any common factors that appear in both the numerator and the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3t-15}{3{t}^{2}-30t+75} & =\\frac{3(t-5)}{3({t}^{2}-10t+25)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(t-5)}{3(t-5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(t-5)}{3(t-5)(t-5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{3}\\cancel{(t-5)}}{\\cancel{3}\\cancel{(t-5)}(t-5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t-5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529170 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115279 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4030a2b3-34aa-5d00-bd95-e382ec781b20" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Rational Expression by Factoring Second-Order Polynomials in Both the Numerator and Denominator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05d0df93-ac65-52bd-b1f7-5efc926ad378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5h+15}{4h-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528316} {:answer/id #uuid "185900a0-b3b8-508d-b13a-d0f1a28cf375" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5h-1}{4h+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528364} {:answer/id #uuid "79ace241-1195-5850-9c3f-c5067cd881cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5h+10}{4h+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528586} {:answer/id #uuid "dc19d4eb-f44e-5b44-98ae-da4ebb739925" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5h-10}{4h+8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528845} {:answer/id #uuid "ea3a3b7d-430a-5e6b-ad81-75063775b9b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5h-15}{4h-8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528879}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea3a3b7d-430a-5e6b-ad81-75063775b9b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5h-15}{4h-8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528879} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce07fe95-9768-5d1e-bdb4-bd567a7424d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529052}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ca2d9c6a-ef62-5982-8134-5f8260bfee4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-113084" :question/problem "$\\frac{5{h}^{2}-10h-15}{4{h}^{2}-4h-8}=$" :question/worked-solution "We factor the numerator and denominator, canceling out any common factors that appear in both.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5{h}^{2}-10h-15}{4{h}^{2}-4h-8} & =\\frac{5({h}^{2}-2h-3)}{4({h}^{2}-h-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5(h+1)(h-3)}{4(h-2)(h+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cancel{(h+1)}(h-3)}{4(h-2)\\cancel{(h+1)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5(h-3)}{4(h-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5h-15}{4h-8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529185 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115279 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4030a2b3-34aa-5d00-bd95-e382ec781b20" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Rational Expression by Factoring Second-Order Polynomials in Both the Numerator and Denominator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d02cd7b-0c89-50c8-a354-474f0af1ffff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{b-2}{4b+14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528455} {:answer/id #uuid "5a70ca19-e1f1-5782-b3eb-5cb3bd61d5f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{b+4}{4b+6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528512} {:answer/id #uuid "603bb21b-1525-5e2c-8f15-00663cd88f35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{b-3}{4b+8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528527} {:answer/id #uuid "9dbe3d10-5061-528e-81f8-39432f7bfbb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{b+3}{4b-12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528678} {:answer/id #uuid "e3332cc0-b4ea-572e-b440-6236bbb8d4db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{b-4}{4b+28}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3332cc0-b4ea-572e-b440-6236bbb8d4db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{b-4}{4b+28}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528859} :answer-field/id #uuid "02dbfdaf-c00e-5aee-95f8-716944a85088" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528938}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e14ac645-6583-57f4-8d3d-7907bb61243a" :question/math-academy-id "q-113086" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $\\frac{{b}^{2}-7b+12}{4{b}^{2}+16b-84}?$" :question/worked-solution "We factor the numerator and denominator, canceling out any common factors that appear in both.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{b}^{2}-7b+12}{4{b}^{2}+16b-84} & =\\frac{{b}^{2}-7b+12}{4({b}^{2}+4b-21)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(b-3)(b-4)}{4(b+7)(b-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(b-3)}(b-4)}{4(b+7)\\cancel{(b-3)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{b-4}{4(b+7)} \\\\  & =\\frac{b-4}{4b+28}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529172 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115271 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6af60bcc-de12-52a1-b0b0-9485ed497126" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Rational Expression by Factoring a Difference of Squares in the Numerator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a4bb1f4-698f-5f7a-838a-5ebcefe0a02e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528370} {:answer/id #uuid "20fc4279-4daa-5993-bbfc-4fe6c0dc7985" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(d-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528391} {:answer/id #uuid "45759f13-683a-52b2-9937-1f0e2e644b52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2d+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528474} {:answer/id #uuid "a1e6d992-f846-5567-83a6-5821d896ca7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "d-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528690} {:answer/id #uuid "b8dcb63b-a726-5a54-a40e-08b2a042b5c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "d+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528749}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20fc4279-4daa-5993-bbfc-4fe6c0dc7985" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(d-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528391} :answer-field/id #uuid "30c89f43-fe1c-589d-a88c-d3627040f00f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528970}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cd81b926-79ef-579e-9c6d-82f75c5992d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-14337" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $\\frac{4{d}^{2}-36}{2(d+3)}?$" :question/worked-solution "The numerator is a difference of squares. It can be factored as\n\n$$\n4{d}^{2}-36=4({d}^{2}-9)=4(d+3)(d-3).\n$$\n\nCanceling out any common factors that appear in the numerator and the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4{d}^{2}-36}{2(d+3)} & = \\\\ \\frac{4(d+3)(d-3)}{2(d+3)} & = \\\\ \\frac{2\\cdot \\cancel{2(d+3)}(d-3)}{\\cancel{2(d+3)}} & = \\\\ 2(d-3).\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115505 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115279 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4030a2b3-34aa-5d00-bd95-e382ec781b20" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Rational Expression by Factoring Second-Order Polynomials in Both the Numerator and Denominator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a4c56f8-ce4c-5391-98e3-49ec1d8a6d45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}-3}{{y}^{2}-2y+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528406} {:answer/id #uuid "3a93a5c9-9b97-50c8-a9d7-889c73728a64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y-3}{y+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528449} {:answer/id #uuid "a53452b3-ec60-5862-88ef-57f3f210e854" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528698} {:answer/id #uuid "d6fcaa55-a5ac-5cf9-823b-bfaa2dc9ba68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}-9}{{y}^{2}-6y+9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528835} {:answer/id #uuid "f0b0bba3-a44d-5fed-b627-cf10eb5ab4e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y+3}{y-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528894}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0b0bba3-a44d-5fed-b627-cf10eb5ab4e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y+3}{y-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528894} :answer-field/id #uuid "8abb5688-150a-50b2-9719-9f49715e34e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112039}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6dd5bac7-d40e-5521-a7ba-7380ff2d57e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-150" :question/problem "What is $\\frac{{y}^{2}-9}{{y}^{2}-6y+9}$ reduced to lowest terms?" :question/worked-solution "We factor the numerator and denominator, canceling out any common factors that appear in both.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}-9}{{y}^{2}-6y+9} & =\\frac{(y+3)(y-3)}{(y-3)(y-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(y+3)\\cancel{(y-3)}}{(y-3)\\cancel{(y-3)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{y+3}{y-3}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529110 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca7321f2-f17f-5d22-a0d1-02720b3a6dc5" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Rational Expression by Factoring a Second-Order Polynomial in the Denominator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "756a6803-8e24-5a8f-81c5-20f6d39dcb43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a-b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528570} {:answer/id #uuid "8e6cdf5e-b7eb-5794-be85-9572ba174c02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7a-b}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528641} {:answer/id #uuid "9e70a9d6-bacc-5fe2-8568-8f05a6c6178d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7(a-b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528680} {:answer/id #uuid "affb3ad8-1d5d-58a4-a1b4-565b6899a4b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7(a-b)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528727} {:answer/id #uuid "f66f70aa-4cfe-5c9a-8e5d-f20fca2a0a07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7a-b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "affb3ad8-1d5d-58a4-a1b4-565b6899a4b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7(a-b)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528727} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b49dace-7157-5fcd-93a6-38c7a216f0bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528964}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "33d475f4-4da4-572d-a596-bce698fbb9fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-29819" :question/problem "$\\frac{a+b}{7{a}^{2}-7{b}^{2}}=$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator can be factored as the difference of squares: \n\n$$\n7{a}^{2}-7{b}^{2}=7({a}^{2}-{b}^{2})=7(a+b)(a-b)\n$$\n\nCanceling out any common factors that appear in both the numerator and the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a+b}{7{a}^{2}-7{b}^{2}} & =\\frac{a+b}{7(a+b)(a-b)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(a+b)}}{7\\cancel{(a+b)}(a-b)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7(a-b)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529154 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115272 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22de4ff5-a317-5d89-a9da-80d40648f2e1" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Rational Expression by Factoring a Second-Order Polynomial in the Numerator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d1bf402-2afb-5c64-b896-4ce5b25191f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528596} {:answer/id #uuid "8cd4341e-9e1f-57a3-92b6-47f9dac335fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528636} {:answer/id #uuid "9b9a62e1-10e7-5aae-b24c-ef6c91fb4783" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2z-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528673} {:answer/id #uuid "9ea4ea88-52b2-5117-87dd-c779eb9c4fc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(z+3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528681} {:answer/id #uuid "a7db0885-9857-59ef-aa12-19ff2e1e8055" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528708}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8cd4341e-9e1f-57a3-92b6-47f9dac335fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528636} :answer-field/id #uuid "71fe9ac9-190b-5ddf-9a82-dec2c9c13572" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529006}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "97b7ba7e-3c98-5de8-abc1-d6b6edb5c45e" :question/math-academy-id "q-29824" :question/problem "What is $\\frac{{z}^{2}-6z+9}{3-z}$ reduced to lowest terms?" :question/worked-solution "The numerator can be factored as\n\n$$\n{z}^{2}-6z+9=(z-3)^{2}.\n$$\n\nCanceling out any common factors that appear in the numerator and the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{z}^{2}-6z+9}{3-z} & = \\\\ -\\frac{{z}^{2}-6z+9}{z-3} & = \\\\ -\\frac{(z-3)^{2}}{z-3} & = \\\\ -\\frac{\\cancel{(z-3)}(z-3)}{\\cancel{z-3}} & = \\\\ -\\frac{z-3}{1} & = \\\\ 3-z. & \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529098 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115272 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22de4ff5-a317-5d89-a9da-80d40648f2e1" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Rational Expression by Factoring a Second-Order Polynomial in the Numerator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d457d92-6320-53f2-9315-874942a29b8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528379} {:answer/id #uuid "44b8beec-f4c9-56f5-8f2d-a07c2d57977e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528473} {:answer/id #uuid "8bf7a3f0-c0df-5b8c-b400-8e794d4bb35b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(x-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528635} {:answer/id #uuid "9283e316-d4bf-5c6f-a1c8-9188e0ef934f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528649} {:answer/id #uuid "b5016bc6-f834-5ac4-9707-8c7e7f29884f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d457d92-6320-53f2-9315-874942a29b8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528379} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd54c305-6b0a-5ce5-906d-173086ca26a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529064}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1950cd5e-6ddb-5e2d-959e-224740d86f48" :question/math-academy-id "q-32322" :question/problem "Simplify $\\frac{4{x}^{2}-8x+4}{4x-4}.$" :question/worked-solution "The numerator can be factored as\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}-8x+4=4({x}^{2}-2x+1)=4(x-1)^{2}.\n$$\n\nCanceling out any common factors that appear in the numerator and the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4{x}^{2}-8x+4}{4x-4} & = \\\\ \\frac{4(x-1)^{2}}{4(x-1)} & = \\\\ \\frac{4(x-1)(x-1)}{4(x-1)} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{4(x-1)}(x-1)}{\\cancel{4(x-1)}} & = \\\\ \\frac{x-1}{1} & = \\\\ x-1. & \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529173 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115271 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6af60bcc-de12-52a1-b0b0-9485ed497126" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Rational Expression by Factoring a Difference of Squares in the Numerator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01fb7c10-16da-5655-89a8-0db41c13a85c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x+5}{2x+5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528303} {:answer/id #uuid "761d8a8e-8e20-5d48-8b7b-85f1706249d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x+5}{x-5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528573} {:answer/id #uuid "8b27e861-ad1c-53e3-8dca-2bd5b29ee53f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{x+5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528632} {:answer/id #uuid "d36771b1-f1e2-52aa-a80d-d81f90312d27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x+5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528829} {:answer/id #uuid "f3833a21-5e72-5d36-abd2-635091490dce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x-5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3833a21-5e72-5d36-abd2-635091490dce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x-5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528899} :answer-field/id #uuid "20d16c6a-9c80-50fb-bcb4-91fb12d610db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528958}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cf71d35a-0b9f-5563-8501-c0ec218240c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-79518" :question/problem "Simplify $\\frac{{x}^{2}-25}{2x+10}.$" :question/worked-solution "The numerator is a difference of squares. If we factor it and then cancel out any common factors that appear in both the numerator and the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}-25}{2x+10} & = \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)(x+5)}{2(x+5)} & = \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)\\cancel{(x+5)}}{2\\cancel{(x+5)}} & = \\\\ \\frac{x-5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529141 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115279 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4030a2b3-34aa-5d00-bd95-e382ec781b20" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Rational Expression by Factoring Second-Order Polynomials in Both the Numerator and Denominator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "878b8168-4e99-55cf-bfb9-df7740b08e3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{a-2}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528624} {:answer/id #uuid "a940a945-0eb1-5120-b96c-419114e81e79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{a+2}{a-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528712} {:answer/id #uuid "b15102e0-61a5-5171-a2af-da7cbae7775e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{a-2}{a+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528731} {:answer/id #uuid "ca166edf-a07d-5672-8745-9a484f33beca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{a}{a+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528795} {:answer/id #uuid "fcb69b37-dc2f-5790-8ba1-41a7aa979bd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{a+2}{a}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b15102e0-61a5-5171-a2af-da7cbae7775e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{a-2}{a+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528731} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c230db6-7b8d-59da-8017-ad873f367157" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529025}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "77fb920e-43ca-5282-8a0a-596d7af0b021" :question/math-academy-id "q-79524" :question/problem "What is $\\frac{{a}^{2}-4a+4}{{a}^{2}-4}$ reduced to lowest terms?" :question/worked-solution "We factor the numerator and denominator, canceling out any common factors that appear in both.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{a}^{2}-4a+4}{{a}^{2}-4} & =\\frac{(a-2)^{2}}{(a-2)(a+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(a-2)\\cancel{(a-2)}}{\\cancel{(a-2)}(a+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{a-2}{a+2}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
